# Board and trail records



The factory's board as the website reads it: how many problems stand in each
stage, the best-ranked of them, who is contributing, and what a contributor may
focus a worker on.

A problem's trail as the website reads it: every attempt and event, newest
last, flattened for the browser. The canonical entries, with their hash chain,
are `/api/v1/trail/:id`; this is the same history made displayable — the lists an
entry carries are joined into text, because a page cannot decode a record that
holds a list (LOGOS_ISSUES.md 1).

## Note
One stage of the board: its problems, and the units waiting and leased on them.

## A BoardLane has:
    a stage, which is Text.
    a problems, which is Int.
    a readyUnits, which is Int.
    a leasedUnits, which is Int.

## Note
One problem on the board, in its stage's lane, with the unit being worked on it
if one is (`unitKind` and `holder` are the empty text when none is).

## A BoardCard has:
    a problemId, which is Text.
    a title, which is Text.
    a stage, which is Text.
    a rankBp, which is Int.
    a cohort, which is Text.
    a collection, which is Text.
    a unitKind, which is Text.
    a holder, which is Text.

## Note
One contributor: attempts made, proofs claimed and proofs the verifier attested,
dead ends found (each saves everyone after them a repeat), and what they spent of
the budget they set. `lastSeen` is the Unix milliseconds of their latest attempt.

## A LeaderRow has:
    a contributor, which is Text.
    a displayName, which is Text.
    an attempts, which is Int.
    a claimed, which is Int.
    an attested, which is Int.
    a deadEnds, which is Int.
    a spentMicros, which is Int.
    a budgetMicros, which is Int.
    a lastSeen, which is Int.

## Note
A focus a contributor may give a worker: a cohort or a collection, with the
problems it holds. `value` is what goes in `MACSAD_FOCUS`.

## A FocusOption has:
    a value, which is Text.
    a label, which is Text.
    a kind, which is Text.
    a problems, which is Int.

## Note
Whether the coordinator can serve: whether its database answers (`database` is
`reachable` or what went wrong), and how much the factory holds.

## A HealthView has:
    an ok, which is Bool.
    a database, which is Text.
    a problems, which is Int.
    a readyUnits, which is Int.
    a leasedUnits, which is Int.
    an attempts, which is Int.
    a trailEntries, which is Int.
    an attested, which is Int.

## Note
One trail entry. `suggestions` joins the entry's next suggestions with ` · `,
and `artifacts` counts the files it names; `hash` and `prevHash` are its links.

## A TrailRow has:
    a seq, which is Int.
    a ts, which is Int.
    a stage, which is Text.
    a kind, which is Text.
    a contributor, which is Text.
    a model, which is Text.
    a strategyId, which is Text.
    a verdict, which is Text.
    an exitCode, which is Int.
    a diagnostics, which is Text.
    a costMicros, which is Int.
    a summary, which is Text.
    a suggestions, which is Text.
    an artifacts, which is Int.
    a fingerprint, which is Text.
    a hash, which is Text.
    a prevHash, which is Text.
